{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105753","id":2481787148,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6T7REM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105753","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105753.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105753.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105753","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105753/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105753/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105753/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d0481b0cba2dd72f42892a088c860cbb479eea28","number":105753,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Rename `String::size` to `String::buffer_size`, to prevent misinterpretation. Use `length()` instead where appropriate.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Supersedes #105710. \r\n\r\n`String::size` is error prone and misleading. I am proposing to rename it to `buffer_size` to make its purpose clearer.\r\n`String::size` is luckily not exposed to GDExtension or GDScript.\r\n\r\nThis PR is likely to both fix subtle bugs and cause regressions (though less likely than #105710). I recommend merging it soon (early in the 4.5 release cycle).\r\n\r\n## Explanation\r\n\r\nI was investigating why https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102369 failed, when I realized that empty strings have a dichotomous state:\r\n- `_cowdata` is empty (`_ptr == nullptr`)\r\n- `_cowdata` is allocated and `_size` is 1. The only character is used for the trailing 0 (`NUL` terminator).\r\n\r\nThis peculiarity does not seem to be widely known. It is currently common to check for `String` emptiness like this:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/931820d33cbc38328e4014d65dd62c359b5116fc/drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp#L179\r\n\r\nThis is incorrect because the `String` in question might be empty but allocated, whereupon `size()` would return 1. It should call `if (p_version->uniforms.length())` instead (or better, `if (!p_version->uniforms.is_empty())`).\r\n\r\nAdditionally, `size` is currently often mistaken for `length` in the codebase. While making this PR, I found many subtle bugs of code that was iterating over the trailing `NUL` character and (potentially) inserting it into strings or other data.\r\n\r\nBy renaming to `buffer_size`, it's clearer that this should only be used when interacting with the buffer directly (such as when using `resize` and filling contents).\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\nInterface:\r\n- `size()` is renamed to `buffer_size()` in `ustring.h`\r\n- A related unit test was edited to do more\r\n- `get_data()` is moved to the header to allow inlining.\r\n\r\nCallers:\r\n- `size() - 1` is almost always replaced by `length()`\r\n- `if (size())` is replaced by `if (length())` (could be `!is_empty` but that's out of scope)\r\n- `size()` is replaced by `length()` if it is obviously more correct\r\n- `size()` is replaced by `buffer_size()` in other cases.\r\n\r\n## Addendum\r\n\r\nWe should resolve the dichotomy mentioned above. Empty `String`s should not allocate. Without the dichotomy, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102369 can also be merged for a pretty significant speed boost.\r\nThis will unfortunately require a little bit of a compatibility breakage, so I wanted to do this PR first.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","description":"","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://a